  "_comment": [
    "Baseline for scripts/lint_fenced_code.mjs (issue #457).",
    "",
    "assumedContext -- identifiers the surrounding PROSE establishes rather than any",
    "fence. Deliberately tiny, and every entry is derived from a measured pattern in",
    "this corpus, not from a generic browser-globals wish list. Note what is NOT here:",
    "gsap, THREE, ScrollTrigger, Flip, Draggable and the rest of the library surface",
    "were resolved structurally by the skill-directory import rule (90 gsap findings",
    "went to zero), so hard-coding them would be both redundant and stale.",
    "",
    "trackedFindings -- the pre-existing corpus, baselined per file by identifier name",
    "so the gate is green on master and ratchets: a NEW undeclared identifier in any",
    "of these files still fails. These are real findings, not false positives; the",
    "decision to fix them belongs to the orchestrator because several live in files",
    "pinned by the vendorization lock. Keyed by name rather than line so ordinary",
    "line drift does not churn the baseline.",
    "",
    "unparseableBlocks -- fences that do not parse, so they were never scope-analyzed.",
    "Recorded rather than swallowed: an unanalyzed block is an open hole, and hiding",
    "it would be the silent fail-open of issue #452. Keyed by block index within the",
    "file (document order), which is stable under edits inside a block.",
    "",
    "Regenerate with: node scripts/lint_fenced_code.mjs --update-allowlist"
  ],
